{
  "dom_id": "step-q93260",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249141/assets/4ae8d09f2e4bca084d113aaa06f80570da8d628868ccd3c9c208337de303d068.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the triangular prism represented by the net above?",
  "worked_solution": "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 8+3\\times 30 \\\\  & =16+90 \\\\  & =106\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
